{"type":"after","callId":"jgqi@4462","endTime":363939.372,"result":{"value":"All projects\nMOBILE EXPERIENCE / 07\nPace of Play.\n\nA golf application presentation combining course maps, pace indicators, score information, and round details.\n\nPROJECT TYPE\nMobile apps\nFOCUS\nGolf & course activity\nORIGINAL PROJECT ARTWORK\nOverview\nKey features\nDesign\nScreenshots\n01\nPROJECT OVERVIEW\nSee the round in its course context.\n\nPace of Play’s artwork describes tracking play with crowdsourced information. The supplied screens pair aerial golf-course views with a pace gauge and detailed round information. A scorecard-style interface adds a more structured view to the map-led presentation.\n\n02\nKEY FEATURES\nA closer look at\nthe experience.\n\nThe flows and interface elements visible in Pace of Play's original project material.\n\n01\nCourse maps\n\nAerial course views establish the geographical context.\n\n02\nPace indicator\n\nA gauge visualizes the displayed pace information.\n\n03\nRound details\n\nDedicated panels organize information about the round.\n\n04\nScorecard layout\n\nA structured grid presents hole-by-hole information.\n\n03\nDESIGN DIRECTION\nIts own identity.\nIn every detail.\nGolf & course activity\n\nDeep green connects the interface to the course setting. Large map surfaces establish context, while a multicolored gauge creates a strong focal point for pace information. White score panels make dense round details easier to scan.\n\nDesign observations from the supplied project artwork.\n04\nUI SCREENSHOTS & ARTWORK\nInside Pace of Play.\n\nExplore the original interface screens. Select any image for a closer look.\n\nINTERFACE SCREEN\n01\nINTERFACE SCREEN\n02\nINTERFACE SCREEN\n03\nINTERFACE SCREEN\n04\nSOURCE MATERIAL\n\nProject descriptions are based on the published artwork and available overview. Interface observations do not imply verified implementation details or measured business results.\n\nOriginal project page\nNEXT MOBILE PROJECT\nQcop App\nKEEP EXPLORING\nMore perspectives.\nView all work\nWORK RECORDS & DOCUMENTS\nQcop App\nFAMILY & DAILY CARE\nLittle Butterflies\nCASE OPERATIONS\nCase Management ASE\nHAVE A PROJECT IN MIND?\nLet's make your\nnext idea real.\nBook a free consultation"}}
